            "subject": "Show what a saving or debt is tracking on its detail screen",
            "body": "Show what a saving or debt is tracking on its detail screen\n\nCategories, bank accounts, auto-sync and the calculation rules could be set when\ncreating or editing a saving/debt and then never seen again — the detail screen\nshowed name, amounts, goals and notes only, so there was no way to check what a\ngoal was actually watching without opening the edit modal.\n\nTrackingSummaryCard is a read-only mirror of AdvancedFinanceSettings, shared by\nboth detail screens. It renders nothing when none of it is configured, and lists\nonly the calculation rules that differ from the variant's template — four rows\nof defaults would be noise on every screen.\n\nVerified on the simulator against a real saving (auto-sync on, one category, one\naccount). The debt variant differs only in its defaults and its calcOptions\nnamespace, and could not be exercised: the account has no debts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
            "author": {
